---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { page, breadcrumb } from '../lib/seo';
const schema = [page('WebPage', { site:Astro.site, path:'/quickstart', name:'Safe first local-AI test', description:'A cautious first-run checklist using synthetic or public text.' }), breadcrumb(Astro.site, [{name:'Quickstart',path:'/quickstart'}])];
---
<Base title="Safe first local-AI test" description="A cautious first-run checklist using synthetic or public text." appearance="light" schema={schema}>
  <header class="gf-page-hero"><div class="gf-shell"><p class="gf-eyebrow">Quickstart</p><h1 class="gf-display mt-4">Run a harmless first test.</h1><p class="gf-lede">Learn the mechanics with synthetic or public text before you consider any professional workflow. Do not paste a real client, patient, employee, or account document into an unfamiliar tool.</p></div></header>
  <section class="gf-content"><div class="gf-shell max-w-4xl"><div class="gf-method"><div><span>01</span><h2>Check the machine</h2><p>Find unified memory under Apple menu → About This Mac, then use the planning checker.</p><a class="gf-link inline-flex mt-4" href="/setup">Open the checker →</a></div><div><span>02</span><h2>Inspect the complete data path</h2><p>Know the runtime, model artifact, network behavior, logs, plugins, sync, and backups. “Local model” does not mean the whole system is offline.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h2>Use a safe fixture</h2><p>Try invented or public source material. Save the exact prompt and inspect omissions and unsupported additions.</p></div></div><div class="gf-boundary-grid mt-12"><div><h3>A first run can teach</h3><ul><li>Whether the runtime starts.</li><li>Whether the artifact plausibly fits memory.</li><li>How the interface and output behave.</li></ul></div><div><h3>It cannot prove</h3><ul><li>Professional accuracy or usefulness.</li><li>Security, privacy, or compliance.</li><li>Performance on sensitive real-world work.</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
</Base>
